.SH "NAME"
Docv::Color \- A terminal color: the default color, an entry of the terminal\(aqs 256\-color palette (0\-15 are the ANSI colors of the terminal theme) or a 24\-bit RGB value, packed into 32 bits.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv"\fR
.sp
\fBstruct Docv::Color\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
A terminal color: the default color, an entry of the terminal\(aqs 256\-color
palette (0\-15 are the ANSI colors of the terminal theme) or a 24\-bit RGB
value, packed into 32 bits.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBDEFAULT = new(0_u32)\fR
The terminal\(aqs default foreground or background.
.PP
\fBRGB_FLAG = 16777216_u32\fR
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.PP
\fBdef self.new(value : UInt32)\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef self.palette(index : Int) : Color\fR
Palette entry \fIindex\fR (0\-255; 0\-7 are the ANSI colors, 8\-15 their
bright variants).
.TP 4
\fBdef self.rgb(red : Int, green : Int, blue : Int) : Color\fR
A 24\-bit color.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.PP
\fBdef blue : UInt8\fR
.PP
\fBdef default? : Bool\fR
.PP
\fBdef green : UInt8\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef index : Int32\fR
The palette index of a palette color.
.PP
\fBdef palette? : Bool\fR
.PP
\fBdef red : UInt8\fR
.PP
\fBdef rgb? : Bool\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef to_sgr(io : IO, foreground : Bool) : Nil\fR
Writes the SGR parameters selecting this color as the \fIforeground\fR or
background, each after a \fB\%;\fR; nothing for the default color.
.PP
